    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννῠχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			= foreg., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγγελος ἦλθε . . ἔννυχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.716
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Maiist.
				16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. κοῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					11.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					645
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔννυχα λίαν ἀναστάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
					1.35
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aesop.
					110
				</span></i>
			. </div>
